orecast for product 0 and exactly the forecast for product 1.\n  - **4** orders about 1.1× the forecast for both.\n  - **7** orders about 1.2× the forecast for both.\n\n  The demand multiplier averages 1.046, so ordering exactly the forecast tends to run short. For product 0, extra stock is clearly worth it. So I rank 7, 4 and 6 ahead of 2.\n- **3** orders every 3 days with about 1.1× safety stock. It saves about 220 in daily order fees compared with ordering every 2 days. But it holds roughly half a day's demand more in stock, costing about 20 a day, so the plan is probably slightly worse overall.\n- **5** orders daily with a small safety margin (about 1.09×). It pays about 715 more in order fees than the every-2-days plans. That is roughly offset by about 600 less in storage.\n\nCandidates 2, 3 and 5 are close for the fourth place; my estimates for them are 0.38–0.42."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 5048, "cache_read_input_tokens": 886, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 5048}, "output_tokens": 3, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-29T07:58:36.386Z", "request_id": "req_011CgWAzFE6yDCfY7JbiJoVg"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 1}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_start", "index": 2, "content_block": {"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01FoKsSzXeV8csfnChqjktDH", "name": "StructuredOutput", "input": {}, "caller": {"type": "direct"}}}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgWAzFVjPAchwaq5mFYFD", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_